      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785167560740,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This concept becomes even more interesting on Day 2, when we dive into inodes. At that point \nyou'll understand why, in Linux, a filename is actually just a reference to an inode—and why \ndeleting a filename doesn't always mean the underlying data disappears immediately.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This concept becomes even more interesting on Day 2, when we dive into inodes. At that point \nyou'll understand why, in Linux, a filename is actually just a reference to an inode—and why \ndeleting a filename doesn't always mean the underlying data disappears immediately.",
